---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { articlePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqPageSchema, webPageSchema } from "../../utils/schema";

const title = "Stonewalling and Silent Treatment: Stop Chasing, Ask for a Return Time";
const description = "Practical scripts for stonewalling, silent treatment, shutdowns, repair attempts, and the stop-chasing response: one clear message and a return time.";
const canonical = "/guides/stonewalling-silent-treatment-response/";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is silent treatment abuse?",
    "answer": "It can be part of emotional abuse when it is used repeatedly to punish, control, isolate, or force compliance. Not every pause is abuse."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if they genuinely need space?",
    "answer": "Give space and ask for a return time. Space becomes healthier when it has a path back."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I keep texting until they answer?",
    "answer": "Usually no. Send one clear message, then stop chasing."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if I was the one who lost my temper?",
    "answer": "Repair your tone without surrendering the whole issue: “I should not have snapped. I still want to talk about the original point.”"
  }
];
const jsonLd = [
  webPageSchema({ title, description, path: canonical }),
  articlePageSchema({ title, description, path: canonical, section: "Pillar Guide" }),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ name: "Guides", path: "/guides/" }, { name: title, path: canonical }]),
  ...(faqs.length ? [faqPageSchema(faqs, canonical)] : [])
];
const contentHtml = "<section class=\"manual-entry-section related-guide-links\"><p class=\"section-label\">Related Conflict Protocol pages</p><ul><li><a href=\"/situations/reopen-after-silence/\">Reopen After Silence</a></li><li><a href=\"/situations/after-snapping-hold-boundary/\">After Snapping Hold Boundary</a></li><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/boundary/\">Boundary</a></li><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/broken-record/\">Broken Record</a></li></ul></section>\n<h2>Quick answer</h2>\n<p>Stonewalling is shutting down or refusing to engage in a way that blocks resolution.</p>\n<p>Silent treatment is silence used as punishment, control, or pressure.</p>\n<p>Not every pause is stonewalling. Sometimes a pause prevents damage.</p>\n<p>A strong first line is:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m okay with taking a break. I’m not okay with disappearing from the conversation. Let’s choose a time to come back to it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m okay with taking a break. I’m not okay with disappearing from the conversation. Let’s choose a time to come back to it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>That line respects the need to cool down without letting silence become a weapon.</p>\n<h2>Pause vs punishment</h2>\n<p>A healthy pause has a return time.</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m overwhelmed. I need twenty minutes, then I’ll come back.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m overwhelmed. I need twenty minutes, then I’ll come back.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Punishing silence has no path back.</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Forget it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Forget it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>No answer for days.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"No answer for days.\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>Coldness until you apologize for having a limit.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"Coldness until you apologize for having a limit.\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>The difference is not just silence. The difference is whether the silence protects the conversation or controls the other person.</p>\n<p>You can respect a pause.</p>\n<p>You do not have to chase punishment.</p>\n<h2>What stonewalling sounds like</h2>\n<ul><li>“I’m done.”</li><li>“Whatever.”</li><li>“Forget it.”</li><li>“I can’t talk to you.”</li><li>“You should know what you did.”</li><li>“Nothing.”</li><li>“If you cared, you’d figure it out.”</li><li>Silence after you say NO.</li><li>Silence until you soften your boundary.</li></ul>\n<p>The trap is panic-chasing.</p>\n<p>You send one message. Then another. Then a paragraph. Then an apology you do not mean. Then a promise to drop the issue.</p>\n<p>The silence has trained you to negotiate against yourself.</p>\n<h2>What to say</h2>\n<h3>When they need a real break</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Take the break. Let’s come back to this at 7.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Take the break. Let’s come back to this at 7.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they walk away every time</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m okay with pausing. I’m not okay with this never coming back.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m okay with pausing. I’m not okay with this never coming back.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they punish you with silence</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m not going to chase the conversation all night.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m not going to chase the conversation all night.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they say “forget it”</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I don’t want to forget it. I want to pause and return when we can talk clearly.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I don’t want to forget it. I want to pause and return when we can talk clearly.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When you need to reopen later</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I want to return to what happened yesterday. I’m not trying to restart the fight. I want to finish the conversation cleanly.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I want to return to what happened yesterday. I’m not trying to restart the fight. I want to finish the conversation cleanly.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>What to text back</h2>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Short:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m okay with a break. When should we come back to this?”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m okay with a break. When should we come back to this?”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Warmer:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I don’t want to push while you’re overwhelmed. I do want us to choose a time to return to it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I don’t want to push while you’re overwhelmed. I do want us to choose a time to return to it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Firmer:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not going to keep sending messages into silence. I’m available to talk when we can address the issue directly.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not going to keep sending messages into silence. I’m available to talk when we can address the issue directly.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">If they disappear after your boundary:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m open to talking. My answer has not changed.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m open to talking. My answer has not changed.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Do not send:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Fine, ignore me forever. I guess I mean nothing.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Fine, ignore me forever. I guess I mean nothing.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>That is the panic talking. It gives the silence more power.</p>\n<h2>Wrong vs better</h2>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Wrong:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Please just answer me. I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have brought it up. Can we forget it?”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Please just answer me. I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have brought it up. Can we forget it?”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Why it feeds the silence:</p>\n<p>You are paying for a response by surrendering the issue.</p>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Better:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m okay with taking space. I’m not okay with dropping the issue completely. Let’s talk tomorrow at 10.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m okay with taking space. I’m not okay with dropping the issue completely. Let’s talk tomorrow at 10.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Why it works:</p>\n<p>It separates space from avoidance.</p>\n<h2>If they push back</h2>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “I just don’t want to fight.” <strong>You say:</strong> “I don’t want to fight either. That’s why I want a time to talk clearly.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “You always push.” <strong>You say:</strong> “I’m not asking to solve it this second. I’m asking that we return to it.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “Nothing is wrong.” <strong>You say:</strong> “Your silence says something is wrong. I’m open to talking when you can be direct.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “Forget it.” <strong>You say:</strong> “I’m not going to force the conversation. I’m also not pretending it disappeared.”</p>\n<h2>A realistic escalation</h2>\n<ol><li><strong>You:</strong> I want to talk about what happened earlier.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> Forget it.</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I don’t want to force it right now. When can we come back to it?</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> I said forget it. You always push.</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I’m not asking to solve it this second. I’m asking that we do not bury it.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> Do whatever you want.</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I’m going to stop texting tonight. I’m available tomorrow if we can talk directly.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> Silence.</li><li><strong>You, next day:</strong> I’m checking once. I’m still open to talking. I’m not going to chase this all week.</li></ol>\n<h2>Scripts by situation</h2>\n<h3>They need a real break</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Yes, take space. Let’s choose a return time before we pause.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Yes, take space. Let’s choose a return time before we pause.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’d rather pause than damage this. Let’s come back at 8.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’d rather pause than damage this. Let’s come back at 8.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>They use silence after your boundary</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m open to talking. My answer is still the same.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m open to talking. My answer is still the same.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not going to treat silence as a reason to change my answer.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not going to treat silence as a reason to change my answer.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>They disappear by text</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m going to stop messaging now. If you want to talk, suggest a time.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m going to stop messaging now. If you want to talk, suggest a time.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not sending more into silence.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not sending more into silence.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>They shut down in a meeting</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Let’s pause the discussion and capture the open decision in writing.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Let’s pause the discussion and capture the open decision in writing.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“If we cannot resolve it now, we need an owner and a follow-up time.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“If we cannot resolve it now, we need an owner and a follow-up time.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>What not to do</h2>\n<p>Do not send ten messages to pull one answer out of them.</p>\n<p>Do not apologize for the boundary just to end the silence.</p>\n<p>Do not pretend the issue disappeared because the room got cold.</p>\n<p>Do not punish them back with your own silence unless what you mean is: “I need space and I will return at a specific time.”</p>\n<p>Silence plus no return path is pressure.</p>\n<h2>Repair after you were the one who shut down</h2>\n<p>Sometimes you are the person who disappeared.</p>\n<p>Repair without over-explaining:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I shut down earlier. I should have asked for a pause instead of disappearing. I’m ready to talk now if you are.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I shut down earlier. I should have asked for a pause instead of disappearing. I’m ready to talk now if you are.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If you need more time:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m still overwhelmed. I do want to come back to this. Can we talk tomorrow at 6?”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m still overwhelmed. I do want to come back to this. Can we talk tomorrow at 6?”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>The repair is simple: own the shutdown, name the return time, come back.</p>\n<h2>When the script fails</h2>\n<p>If they keep using silence to punish:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not going to keep chasing a conversation that disappears every time I raise an issue.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not going to keep chasing a conversation that disappears every time I raise an issue.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If they return only when you drop the topic:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m glad we’re talking again. I still want to address what happened.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m glad we’re talking again. I still want to address what happened.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If the silence is part of a larger pattern of control, fear, monitoring, or punishment, prioritize support and safety. The goal is not to force a conversation with someone who uses access as control.</p>\n<h2>How to practice this</h2>\n<p>Practice asking for a return time.</p>\n<p>Pressure:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m done.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m done.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Your line:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay. When should we come back to it?”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay. When should we come back to it?”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Pressure:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Never mind.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Never mind.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Your line:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not going to force it now. I do want a time to return.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not going to force it now. I do want a time to return.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>The skill is not chasing. The skill is leaving one clear door open.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Treating all silence as abuse.</li><li>Treating all space as acceptable.</li><li>Chasing until you apologize for your boundary.</li><li>Sending huge texts to someone who is not engaging.</li><li>Refusing to return when you were the one who shut down.</li><li>Confusing a pause with repair.</li></ul>\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>Is silent treatment abuse?</h3>\n<p>It can be part of emotional abuse when it is used repeatedly to punish, control, isolate, or force compliance. Not every pause is abuse.</p>\n<h3>What if they genuinely need space?</h3>\n<p>Give space and ask for a return time. Space becomes healthier when it has a path back.</p>\n<h3>Should I keep texting until they answer?</h3>\n<p>Usually no. Send one clear message, then stop chasing.</p>\n<h3>What if I was the one who lost my temper?</h3>\n<p>Repair your tone without surrendering the whole issue: “I should not have snapped. I still want to talk about the original point.”</p>\n<h2>Extra copy-ready lines</h2>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m okay with a pause. I need a return time.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m okay with a pause. I need a return time.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not going to chase this through silence.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not going to chase this through silence.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m available to talk when we can be direct.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m available to talk when we can be direct.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Space is okay. Disappearing from the issue is not.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Space is okay. Disappearing from the issue is not.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m checking once, then I’m stepping back.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m checking once, then I’m stepping back.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>The stop-chasing rule</h2>\n<p>When someone disappears, one clear message is usually better than ten anxious ones.</p>\n<p>The message should include three things:</p>\n<ol><li>you are open to talking</li><li>you will not chase</li><li>the issue still exists</li></ol>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m not going to keep messaging tonight, and I do still want to address what happened.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m not going to keep messaging tonight, and I do still want to address what happened.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Then stop.</p>\n<p>Stopping is not punishment. It is refusing to feed the silence with panic.</p>\n<h2>How to reopen without begging</h2>\n<p>A reopening message should not sound like you are asking permission to have a concern.</p>\n<p>Weak:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Are you still mad? Can we please just forget this? I hate when we’re like this.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Are you still mad? Can we please just forget this? I hate when we’re like this.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Cleaner:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I want to return to yesterday’s conversation. I’m available tonight after 7 if you’re ready to talk directly.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I want to return to yesterday’s conversation. I’m available tonight after 7 if you’re ready to talk directly.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If they answer with more coldness, do not collapse the issue.</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay. I’m not going to push tonight. I still want to address it when you’re ready.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay. I’m not going to push tonight. I still want to address it when you’re ready.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>If silence is the pattern</h2>\n<p>One episode of shutdown is a problem. A repeated cycle is a pattern.</p>\n<p>The cycle often looks like this:</p>\n<ol><li>you raise an issue</li><li>they shut down</li><li>you panic</li><li>you soften or apologize</li><li>they return</li><li>the issue is never addressed</li></ol>\n<p>If that is the pattern, the line changes:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I notice that when I raise an issue, the conversation disappears until I drop it. I’m not willing to keep resolving conflict that way.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I notice that when I raise an issue, the conversation disappears until I drop it. I’m not willing to keep resolving conflict that way.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>That is not a magic fix. It is a clear naming of the cycle.</p>\n<h2>Short scripts for different kinds of silence</h2>\n<p class=\"section-label\">They need a real break:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Take the break. Please tell me when we’ll come back to it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Take the break. Please tell me when we’ll come back to it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">They leave every time conflict starts:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m noticing we pause, but we do not return. I need us to return.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m noticing we pause, but we do not return. I need us to return.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">They punish you after a NO:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m open to talking. I’m not changing my answer to end the silence.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m open to talking. I’m not changing my answer to end the silence.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">They answer with one-word coldness:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“If you want to talk about what happened, I’m available. If not, I’m going to stop checking in tonight.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“If you want to talk about what happened, I’m available. If not, I’m going to stop checking in tonight.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">They say nothing is wrong:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay. I’m going to take you at your word and stop trying to read silence.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay. I’m going to take you at your word and stop trying to read silence.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>That last line is important. If someone insists nothing is wrong, do not keep interrogating the temperature of the room. Let them own their words.</p>\n<h2>What success looks like</h2>\n<p>Success is not making them talk immediately.</p>\n<p>Success may be that you stop chasing.</p>\n<p>Success may be that you ask for a return time.</p>\n<p>Success may be that you refuse to erase your boundary just because the room got cold.</p>\n<p>Success may be that you repair your own shutdown faster than before.</p>\n<p>Stonewalling and silent treatment create panic because they make connection feel conditional. A clean response gives you one steady move: leave the door open, but stop knocking forever.</p>\n<h2>If you are the chaser</h2>\n<p>If silence makes you panic, do not make the goal “never panic.” Make the goal smaller: one clear message, then stop.</p>\n<p>Write the second message in notes, not in the chat. Wait twenty minutes. Read it again. Most second messages are not new information. They are fear looking for a door.</p>\n<p>Use this instead:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m going to stop messaging now. I’m available when you’re ready to talk directly.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m going to stop messaging now. I’m available when you’re ready to talk directly.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Then do something physical: shower, walk, eat, call someone safe, leave the phone across the room. Your body needs proof that silence is uncomfortable, not fatal.</p>\n<p>That may sound basic. It is basic. Basic is what works when your nervous system is trying to turn one unanswered message into an emergency.</p>\n<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>\n<p>Verified links for context and safety boundaries:</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.gottman.com/blog/the-four-horsemen-stonewalling/\">The Gottman Institute: The Four Horsemen - Stonewalling</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thehotline.org/identify-abuse/power-and-control/\">The National Domestic Violence Hotline: Power and control</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thehotline.org/resources/safety-planning-while-living-with-an-abusive-partner/\">The National Domestic Violence Hotline: Safety planning while living with an abusive partner</a></li></ul>";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image="/assets/situations/reopen-after-silence.webp" bodyClass="editorial-page pillar-guide-page" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="answer-page pillar-guide">
    <header class="page-header shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pillar guide</p>
      <h1>Stonewalling and Silent Treatment: Stop Chasing, Ask for a Return Time</h1>
      <div class="answer-lead">
        <p>{description}</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="shell-narrow article-body" set:html={contentHtml.replace(
      "<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>",
      `<h2>The smallest usable version</h2>
<p>If silence makes you panic, do not make the goal a perfect repair. Make the goal one clear message and a stop.</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m going to stop messaging now.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“I’m open to talking when you’re ready. I’m going to stop messaging now.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If the issue still needs to come back, name that too:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“I do still want to address what happened.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“I do still want to address what happened.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If you need a return time, ask once:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“When should we come back to this?”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“When should we come back to this?”">Copy</button></div>
<p>The smallest usable version is not chasing, not punishing back, and not erasing the issue to make the silence end.</p>
<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>`
    )} />

    <script>
      document.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
        const button = event.target instanceof HTMLElement ? event.target.closest("[data-copy]") : null;
        if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return;
        const text = button.dataset.copy || "";
        if (!text) return;
        await navigator.clipboard?.writeText(text);
        const original = button.textContent;
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = original || "Copy";
        }, 1400);
      });
    </script>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
